WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.318
Filesystems are not simple string maps.

2
00:00:02.318 --> 00:00:09.657
A path may involve symbolic links, hard links, mount points, junctions, case-insensitive matching, different path separators, inherited permissions,

3
00:00:09.657 --> 00:00:12.747
network storage, or metadata that changes over time.

4
00:00:12.747 --> 00:00:18.927
A path that looked acceptable during one check may not refer to the same target later.

5
00:00:18.927 --> 00:00:26.652
Links are especially important for security-sensitive file handling because they separate the path text from the object ultimately accessed.

6
00:00:26.652 --> 00:00:33.991
Metadata can help a program reason about a file, but it should be treated as evidence, not absolute truth.

7
00:00:33.991 --> 00:00:40.558
File size, owner, timestamps, type, and permissions can change between operations if another actor controls the location.

8
00:00:40.558 --> 00:00:48.670
When the distinction matters, use platform APIs that check or open the target in a way that matches the intended guarantee.

9
00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:50.987
Platform differences deserve explicit design attention.

10
00:00:50.987 --> 00:00:57.554
Case sensitivity, reserved names, path length behavior, permission models, rename behavior, sharing rules, and durability guarantees vary.

11
00:00:57.554 --> 00:01:02.189
Code that is safe on one filesystem may be incomplete on another.

12
00:01:02.189 --> 00:01:09.528
Portable C++ can use standard library abstractions for many tasks, but security-sensitive behavior sometimes requires documented platform-specific

13
00:01:09.528 --> 00:01:09.914
handling.

14
00:01:09.914 --> 00:01:11.845
The safer habit is humility.

15
00:01:11.845 --> 00:01:13.004
Document filesystem assumptions.

16
00:01:13.004 --> 00:01:14.549
Keep path policy centralized.

17
00:01:14.549 --> 00:01:18.412
Avoid pretending that a string comparison captures every target decision.

18
00:01:18.412 --> 00:01:25.365
Where the platform provides a more precise operation, use it through a small wrapper with a clear contract.

19
00:01:25.365 --> 00:01:30.000
Tests should include the platforms and filesystem behaviors the product actually supports.
